---
/**
 * Terms of Use (Task 200). Plain language, one idea per section. Facts only Christian can supply are
 * <LegalPlaceholder> marks; scripts/check-legal-release.mjs blocks a production build while any remain.
 * Acceptable use is a section here rather than its own page: the legal research drafts treat it as part of the Terms.
 * Nothing on this page is legal advice; a licensed attorney reviews it before launch (docs/status note, D-pending).
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPlaceholder from '../components/LegalPlaceholder.astro';
import LegalApproval from '../components/LegalApproval.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { legal } from '../config/legal';
import { isLegalPageApproved } from '../config/legalapproval';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout title="terms" description="Terms for using Cueory, including accounts, study content, acceptable use and limits." noindex={!isLegalPageApproved("terms")}>
  <Prose>
    <h1>terms of use</h1>
    <LegalApproval page="terms" />

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is a free study website for nursing students. It helps you study. It is not medical advice, not a
      substitute for your school or faculty, and it comes with no guarantees. Be decent to the site and to other people,
      and we will do our best to keep it useful.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is run by{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="legal entity name and type, for example 'Cueory LLC, an Arizona limited liability company', or 'Christian [surname], doing business as Cueory'" />,
      with a mailing address at <LegalPlaceholder what="business mailing address; a lawyer should say which filings need a physical street address" />.
      "We", "us" and "our" mean that operator. You can reach us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Agreeing to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      By using {site.name}, whether or not you create an account, you agree to these terms, to our{' '}
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>, and to the rules on our <a href="/copyright">copyright page</a>. If you
      don't agree, please don't use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Who may use the site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You must be at least <strong class="key-term">{legal.minimumAge}</strong>{' '}
        years old to create an account or send us anything through the site. The sign-up form tells you this; by
        creating an account you are telling us you meet it, although the form does not yet make you tick a box to say
        so.
      </li>
      <li>Nobody under 13 may create an account or send us personal information, and we don't knowingly collect it.</li>
      <li>
        If we learn that someone under the minimum age has an account, we will close it and delete the data we hold
        for it. If you think that has happened, email us.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Study help, not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on {site.name} is for studying. It is not medical, nursing or clinical advice, and it is not instructions
      for caring for a real person. Never use the site to make a decision about a patient. Your school's curriculum,
      your faculty, your textbooks and your clinical instructors come first; where the site disagrees with them, follow
      them. Our <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> says more.
    </p>

    <h2>No promises about exams or licensure</h2>
    <p>
      We don't promise a grade, a passing score, graduation, a licence or a job. Exam names and publisher names on the
      site identify what a lesson is about; they don't mean that exam board, school or publisher sponsors, endorses or
      is affiliated with {site.name}. Some lessons are samples or works in progress and may not yet have citations or
      review by a licensed nurse; the site says so where that is the case.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An account is optional. Lessons work without one.</li>
      <li>Give us a working email address, and keep your password and two-factor device to yourself.</li>
      <li>One account per person. Don't share it, sell it or use someone else's.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for what happens under your account until you tell us it has been compromised.</li>
      <li>
        You can request deletion on your account page without contacting us. For security, you may need to sign in
        again if your current sign-in is not recent enough. Once the required sign-in check passes, deletion removes
        your account and the linked study data, as the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Use {site.name} to study, lawfully. Don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>try to get around sign-in, access limits, rate limits or someone else's data;</li>
      <li>probe, scan, overload or disrupt the site or the services behind it;</li>
      <li>
        copy, scrape or bulk-download our own lessons, questions, answer keys or other Cueory-owned material, by hand or
        by script, or hammer our servers with automated access; material that carries a CC BY 4.0 credit (the adapted
        textbook text and the anatomy models) is not covered by this and may be reused under its own licence, with
        attribution;
      </li>
      <li>re-sell, re-publish or build a competing product from Cueory-owned content (text, layout, branding);</li>
      <li>upload or send anything unlawful, harassing, infringing, or that contains someone else's private or health information;</li>
      <li>put a real patient's details into a report, comment or any other form;</li>
      <li>impersonate anyone, or misrepresent your connection to {site.name};</li>
      <li>use the site in any way that breaks the law where you are.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you send us</h2>
    <p>
      Two different kinds of things reach us. Your account and study data (your email, display name, setup answers,
      answers, study time and review events) is personal data, handled only as the <a href="/privacy">privacy
      page</a> says; these terms grant us no licence over it. Content you submit, which today means reports and comments
      sent with the "Flag or comment" button, is different: you keep whatever rights you have in it, and you give us a
      worldwide, royalty-free, permanent licence to use, copy, edit and act on it to run and improve {site.name},
      including fixing the content you flagged. Only send what you have the right to send, and never a real patient's
      details. We may remove anything you submit at any time, and we may refuse or remove content on a copyright
      complaint as the <a href="/copyright">copyright page</a> explains.{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="with a lawyer: confirm this licence should cover only submitted feedback and never personal records, and whether a future public-content feature needs its own clause" />
    </p>

    <h2>Our content and our rights</h2>
    <p>
      The lessons, questions, cards, puzzles, design, name and logo that {site.name} made belong to us. Our code is
      public to view on GitHub but is not open source. You may use the site for your own personal, non-commercial
      study; please don't copy, scrape, re-publish or re-sell what is ours. We reserve rights only in what we own.
      Where a piece of material on the site carries a third-party or open licence, such as the open textbook we adapt
      and the anatomy models (both CC BY 4.0), you may reuse that piece under its own licence without asking us, as long
      as you keep the credit, the licence link and any notice of changes that the licence requires. Our branding and
      everything that carries no such notice stay reserved. The <a href="/licenses">licences page</a> lists each
      source.{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="with a lawyer: confirm this wording, and confirm the provenance of each anatomy model before any is published" />
    </p>

    <h2>Free service, as is</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is free. It is provided "as is" and "as available", with no warranty of any kind, express or implied,
      including no warranty that it is accurate, complete, current, fit for a particular purpose, uninterrupted or
      error-free. We may change, pause or close any part of the site at any time. Some places don't allow some of
      these exclusions, so some may not apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
      punitive damages, or for lost data, lost profits or lost opportunities, arising from your use of or inability to
      use {site.name}. To the fullest extent the law allows, our total liability to you for everything arising from the
      site, added together, is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us to use it in the twelve months before the
      claim, which for this free service is zero dollars ($0), or one hundred US dollars ($100). Where the law doesn't
      allow a limit this low, our liability is limited to the smallest amount it does allow. Nothing here limits or
      excludes liability that the law says cannot be limited or excluded, such as for fraud, or for death or personal
      injury caused by negligence where the law does not allow that to be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>Your responsibility to us</h2>
    <p>
      If you misuse {site.name}, break these terms or the law, or infringe someone's rights while using the site, and
      someone makes a claim against us because of it, you agree to defend us and to cover the losses, costs and
      reasonable legal fees that result, to the extent the law allows.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending access</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or close your account, or block your use of the site, at any time and at our discretion,
      including if we think you have broken these terms. Where we reasonably can, we will tell you why. You may stop
      using the site, or delete your account, at any time. The sections on our content, liability, your responsibility
      to us, disputes and governing law survive.
    </p>

    <h2>Supporting Cueory</h2>
    <p>
      The site is free, and it has no payments of its own. If you choose to support us, the support page sends you to
      Ko-fi, where the payment is taken by PayPal or Stripe through Ko-fi's platform under their own terms. We don't process payments, see your card
      details or sell anything on the site, and a tip doesn't buy a feature, a result or a say in the content.
    </p>

    <h2>Other websites and services</h2>
    <p>
      Lesson videos play from YouTube when you tap play, Google handles Google sign-in, and the support page links to
      Ko-fi. Those services have their own terms and privacy rules, which we don't control.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. A change takes effect when we post the new version here with its new effective date,
      and using the site after that date means you accept it. For a change that matters to you (for example to the
      limits on our liability, to disputes or to what you may do on the site) we will also, when practical, put a notice
      on the home page for at least{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="confirm the lead time, for example '14 days'" /> before the new version takes effect. The
      dated versions are kept in the public history of our code.{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="emailing account holders about changes needs a real sending mechanism and a matching line on the privacy page before it can be promised here; today account email is only sign-up confirmation and password reset" />
    </p>

    <h2>Disputes</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a problem with {site.name}, tell us first: send a written notice of the dispute to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> with your name, how to reach you, what happened
      and what you would like us to do. We will do the same if we have a problem with you. Both of us agree to try in
      good faith to sort it out informally for 60 days from that notice before starting any court case.
    </p>
    <p>
      <LegalPlaceholder what="with a lawyer: decide whether to add arbitration and a class-action waiver here, or to leave disputes with the courts named below. Nothing is decided yet, and nothing in this section waives a right until it is." />
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law and venue</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="confirm the governing law; Arizona was proposed by the research drafts but is not decided" />,
      without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. Unless the law where you live gives you a right to sue at home,
      any court case about these terms or the site must be brought in the state or federal courts located in{' '}
      <LegalPlaceholder what="confirm the venue, for example 'Maricopa County, Arizona'" />, and you agree to those
      courts' jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>The rest</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If a court finds part of these terms unenforceable, the rest stays in effect, and that part is applied as far as the law allows.</li>
      <li>If we don't enforce a term right away, we can still enforce it later.</li>
      <li>These terms, the privacy page, the disclaimer and the copyright page are the whole agreement between you and us about the site.</li>
      <li>You may not transfer your rights under these terms; we may transfer ours to whoever runs {site.name} after us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
